  type: SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT
  group_id: {{settlementGroupId}}
  is_public: false
}

docs {
  # Upload Settlement Receipt

  - **Method** `POST`
  - **Endpoint** `/api/v1/attachments/upload`
  - **Auth** Bearer access token

  ## Description

  Uploads one private file for an active caller and returns the attachment ID. Add `data.id` to `attachment_ids` in Create Settlement. Only the uploader can bind an unlinked file, and a linked payment receipt is locked for direct edits or deletion. Before linking, access belongs to the uploader. Bruno prompts for a local file when you open the multipart form.

  The server detects MIME from the bytes. It accepts detected `image/*` or `application/pdf`, with a limit of 10 MiB (10,485,760 bytes). If you include `group_id`, the caller must be an active member and the group must be `ACTIVE` or `SETTLING`. Omit the field entirely for a staged receipt without group context.

  ## Enum values

  | Field | Values | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `type` | `SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT` | Receipt category to use with this request. |
  | `group status when group_id is supplied` | `ACTIVE`, `SETTLING` | Accepted group lifecycle states. |

  ## Request

  ### Headers
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Yes | Bearer access token (`Bearer <token>`). |
  | `Content-Type` | `string` | Yes | `multipart/form-data`. Let the HTTP client add the boundary. |

  ### Path parameters
  This endpoint has no path parameters.

  ### Query parameters
  This endpoint has no query parameters.

  ### Body
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `file` | `file` | Yes | One non-empty image or PDF, up to 10 MiB. |
  | `type` | `string` | Yes | Send `SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT`. |
  | `group_id` | `integer` | No | Group for optional membership and lifecycle validation. This Bruno request uses `settlementGroupId`. |
  | `is_public` | `boolean` | No | The server always stores receipts as private. |
  | `expense_id / settlement_id` | `integer` | Omit | Link the file when saving its expense or payment. Supplying either ID returns `BAD_REQUEST`. |

  Example multipart fields with a PDF selected in the `file` control.

  ```text
  file      receipt.pdf
  type      SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT
  group_id  10
  is_public false
  ```

  ## Response

  **`201 Created`**

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 1301,
      "uploaded_by_user_id": 130,
      "group_id": 10,
      "type": "SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT",
      "original_filename": "receipt.pdf",
      "object_key": "attachments/settlement_receipt/130/2026/11/example_receipt.pdf",
      "mime_type": "application/pdf",
      "file_size_bytes": 28413,
      "file_hash": "14eaf9d8d862296aae97f8fd2963967b0c0f02553bc515ea28fa337ab78e7fb8",
      "is_public": false,
      "access_url": "https://storage.example.com/signed/receipt.pdf",
      "uploaded_at": "2026-11-20T09:15:00Z",
      "created_at": "2026-11-20T09:15:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-20T09:15:00Z"
    }
  }
  ```

  ### Response fields

  | Field | Type | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `id` | `integer` | Receipt ID to place in `attachment_ids`. |
  | `uploaded_by_user_id` | `integer` | Authenticated uploader's user ID. |
  | `group_id` | `integer (optional)` | Returned when supplied. |
  | `type` | `string` | Receipt type. |
  | `original_filename` | `string` | Original filename from the uploading client. |
  | `object_key` | `string` | Storage identifier. Use the attachment ID for API operations. |
  | `mime_type` | `string` | MIME type detected from the content. |
  | `file_size_bytes` | `integer` | Number of bytes received. |
  | `file_hash` | `string` | SHA-256 hex digest of the uploaded bytes. |
  | `width / height` | `integer (optional)` | Image dimensions when the server can decode them. Omitted for PDFs. |
  | `is_public` | `boolean` | Always false for receipts. |
  | `access_url` | `string` | Temporary download URL. Can be an empty string if signing fails after upload. |
  | `uploaded_at / created_at / updated_at` | `RFC 3339 timestamp` | Upload, record creation and last change. |

  An unlinked receipt response omits `settlement_id`. The example URL is illustrative.

  ## Errors

  | HTTP | code | error | When it happens |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | 400 | `BAD_REQUEST` | `bad request payload or parameters` | Invalid multipart data, missing or unreadable file, zero bytes, invalid form value or supplied expense_id/settlement_id. |
  | 400 | `INVALID_FILE_TYPE` | `file type or format is not supported` | Unrecognized type or detected bytes are outside the supported image/PDF types. |
  | 400 | `GROUP_INVALID_STATUS` | `status must be ACTIVE, SETTLING or CLOSED` | The supplied group is outside the allowed upload states for this receipt. |
  | 401 | `MISSING_TOKEN` | `authorization token is missing` | Missing Authorization header or invalid Bearer header format. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_INVALID` | `authorization token is invalid` | Invalid access token, including use of a refresh token in its place. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_EXPIRED` | `authorization token has expired` | Access token expired. Refresh it or sign in again. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_REVOKED` | `authorization token has been revoked` | Access token is blacklisted. |
  | 403 | `USER_INACTIVE` | `user account is deactivated` | Caller account is inactive. |
  | 403 | `GROUP_FORBIDDEN` | `you do not have permission to access this group` | The uploader lacks active membership in the supplied group. |
  | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `user not found` | Caller account is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 404 | `GROUP_NOT_FOUND` | `group not found` | Group is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 413 | `FILE_TOO_LARGE` | `file size exceeds maximum allowed limit` | File exceeds 10 MiB. |
  | 500 | `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` | `an internal server error occurred` | Database, transaction or token verification dependency failed. |
  | 503 | `STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE` | `storage service is temporarily unavailable` | Writing the file to storage failed. |

  ### `413 FILE_TOO_LARGE` example

  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "code": "FILE_TOO_LARGE",
    "error": "file size exceeds maximum allowed limit"
  }
  ```
}
